## Step 6: How cache_control Is Sent to API

The function `buildSystemPromptBlocks()` in `src/services/api/claude.ts` (line 3213) converts blocks into the final API format:

```
ACTUAL CODE: src/services/api/claude.ts (line 3213-3237)

  function buildSystemPromptBlocks(systemPrompt, enablePromptCaching) {
    return splitSysPromptPrefix(systemPrompt).map(block => {
      return {
        type: 'text',
        text: block.text,

        // Add cache_control only if caching is enabled AND scope is set
        ...(enablePromptCaching && block.cacheScope !== null && {
          cache_control: getCacheControl({
            scope: block.cacheScope,   // 'global' or 'org'
          }),
        }),
      }
    })
  }


WHAT GETS SENT TO THE API:

  system: [
    {
      type: "text",
      text: "You are Claude Code...[all static sections]...",
      cache_control: {
        type: "ephemeral",
        scope: "global",     ← shared across ALL Claude Code users
        ttl: "1h"            ← cache lives for 1 hour
      }
    },
    {
      type: "text",
      text: "Memory...[all dynamic sections]..."
      // NO cache_control → not cached
    }
  ]
```

