## Step 12: Tool Schema Caching (Bonus)

Not just the prompt — tool definitions are also cached:

```
ACTUAL CODE: src/utils/api.ts (line 119-208)

  async function toolToAPISchema(tool) {
    // Cache key = tool name (or name:schema for dynamic tools)
    const cacheKey = tool.inputJSONSchema
      ? `${tool.name}:${JSON.stringify(tool.inputJSONSchema)}`
      : tool.name

    const cache = getToolSchemaCache()

    // Check cache first
    let base = cache.get(cacheKey)
    if (!base) {
      // Cache miss: compute schema
      base = {
        name: tool.name,
        description: await tool.prompt(),
        input_schema: zodToJsonSchema(tool.inputSchema),
      }
      cache.set(cacheKey, base)   // save for next turn
    }

    return base   // cache hit: instant
  }


  WHY: 40+ tools × schema computation = expensive
       Cache once, reuse every turn.
       Also prevents mid-session schema drift from feature flag flips.
```

